window.products.push({"id":360904,"name":"RAJ GHARANA METALS Pure Kansa (Bronze) Dinner Set - 6 Pcs KANSA Utensils Set - 1 Thali (platter) Dai 12 inch, 2 Bowl (Katori), 1 Sweet Dish, 1 Glass(t","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71zee1t4vbL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Raj Gharana Metal forging precious metal dinner set and kitchenware item from years of generations, Our Indian handmade dinner set has been crafted by very skilled and professional artisans which is highly durable and corrosion and stain resistant. It is ideal for daily usage to serve any food. Raj Gharana Metals Present New Matte Finished Kansa Bronze Dinner Set-6pc 12 inch Weight — 56.43 Oz . It Is The Healing Metal of India – Kansa . The metal Kansa is an alloy of copper and tin. Known in the West as bronze, it was the first of humanity’s metal alloys – and perhaps the most significant. Kansa, or bronze as we would name it, revolutionized the ancient world in many ways. Kansa has many uses; for utensils and implements used in ceremonies. Along with these uses, there has been the tradition of Ayurvedic physicians recommending the use of Kansa on the feet for their clients. Traditional value Kansa usage dates back to thousands of years and have been an integral part of many households till recent years. Kansa basana as it is known traditionally was used in every household across and most parts of western india Ayurveda has documented immense health benefits of using kansa vessel in day-to-day food preparation and serving.  KANSA DINNER SET FEATURES: * Handcrafted and Classic Design* Durable and strudy bronze alloy* Health Benifits* Forged by Indian artisans* Ideal GiftTraditionally it was considered best to have food in kansa plates The process of making starts with making metal ingots with 78-80 % copper and 22-20 % tin mixture. The ingot is then repeatedly heated and beaten by a group of artisans to specific shapes. The finer finishing is done using rubber headed hammers and then a coating of salt and clay applied to firm up the metal. Then the kansa ware is worked with fine hammers and lathe work to give the shine and finish. It takes 23 operations to make one kansa ware This highly skilled craft takes years of","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71zee1t4vbL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"RAJ GHARANA METALS","source_asin":"B096P6MWPZ","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-360904","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B096P6MWPZ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B096P6MWPZ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
